  "term": "divergent thinking",
  "definition": "Divergent thinking is the ability to produce many different, original ideas or responses to a prompt. It emphasizes generating ideas broadly, including speed, variety, uniqueness, and developing ideas further, and is an important part of creativity and solving new problems.",
